    "created_at": "2019-06-26T13:45:17Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-06-26T13:45:17Z",
    "body": "> Isn't an \"abort when\" block really just a hidden loop wherein you're evaluating whether the abort condition is met in between the steps of the algorithm you're executing?\r\n\r\nYep. But if the condition becomes true, it only skips the rest of its inner steps, which is different to \"abort these steps\", which cancels the whole synchronously executing algorithm.",
